From 61e1401298cc5599580b7ed49b93f3577e276af7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Zim <info@zimcontent.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:16:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(runner): a frame says the size of the page it shows,
 so a click lands

A person in control could type but not click, and the page looked
enlarged. agent-browser labels every frame of its stream 1280x720 (and
says the same in its status) whatever the page's size, and the apps map a
click on the picture with that label. On a sign-in window 500 pixels wide
a click on the email field went out 2.5 times too far.

Each frame now goes out with the size of its own picture, which is the
page's on a screen of density 1 that fits the stream (headless, and the
agents' desktops). With a person in control the tab says its size itself
(Page.getLayoutMetrics on its socket), read once per tab and picture
size. The first picture of an idle page says the size the page answers,
not the status's. ADR 0040 section 18.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
